The percentage of total tree canopy cover (TTCC) per block group was calculated using the zonal histogram tool in QGIS [@qgis.org2026]. TTCC represents the total amount of tree canopy cover within a block group, including trees in private yards, businesses, and parks. Public park polygons were then clipped from the land cover raster to calculate the percentage of private tree canopy cover (PTCC) for each block group. PTCC represents the amount of tree canopy cover supplied by trees that are not within public parks.

The Mann-Whitney *U* test was performed to determine whether TTCC within block groups is affected by the presence of public parks. The median TTCC value of the 176 block groups with parks was compared to the TTCC value of the 841block groups without parks, and the *U* statistic was calculated.

The Wilcoxon signed-rank test was performed on the block groups that contain public parks to determine whether the parks contribute to the total tree canopy cover.

### Demographic factors {#sec-demographic}

Total population and race/ethnicity data at the block group level were sourced from the 2024 American Community Survey (ACS) 5-year estimate [@uscensusbureau] using tidycensus. These factors were used to calculate the percentage of Black and Hispanic residents per block group.

The area deprivation index (ADI) at the block group level was acquired from the University of Wisconsin School of Medicine Public Health [-@universityofwisconsinschoolofmedicinepublichealth2023]. The ADI is a validated measure of socioeconomic status based on 17 indicators of income, education, employment, and housing quality [@rollings2023]. The raw ADI score of a block group is compared against all other block groups in the nation and ranked on a percentile scale from 1-100, where 1 indicates the lowest level of disadvantage and 100 indicates the highest disadvantage. Block groups with predominantly group housing (college dormitories or jails) do not have ADI data available, so they were excluded from the analysis. The resulting dataset contained 988 block groups used in the demographic analysis. @fig-bg-parks shows the locations block groups with land cover and/or demographic data available and the public parks within those block groups.

Median household income was considered as an additional explanatory variable, but it was excluded due to its high correlation with ADI rank (*r* = -0.70) and the presence of 50 block groups with suppressed income estimates in the ACS data.


